ember are eligible to receive skill badges — so make sure you sign up on a fresh account for the campaign.2Fill The Enrolment FormRegister through the GeeksforGeeks form. Pick your track, and enter GeeksforGeeks as your partner along with the referral code NRVC72. Developers (working professionals) also add their GEAR / developer profile URL. Watch how to fill the Enrolment Form →3Receive Your Enrolment EmailOnce your enrolment is processed, you'll get a confirmation email with your unique access code.confirmation_numberYou can also get your access code herearrow_forwardschedulePlease check 2 days after registering — access codes are generated in batches, so give it a little time before looking it up.4Redeem Your Access CodeOpen an incognito window, follow the redemption link, and enter your access code. Sign in to Google Skills and you'll see 9 credits ready to go. Follow the walkthrough video →priority_highYour access code is personal, works once, and can't be shared. Use the exact link from your email — searching the catalog won't work.5Complete Your First Lab & Keep GoingOpen "A Tour of Google Cloud Hands-on Labs" and click Start Lab. Follow the steps, spend at least 6 minutes, and aim for a score of 100. When you're done, click End Lab — the 200 free credits are added automatically, no extra claim needed.verifiedCheck your balance at skills.google/my_account/credits. Then work through your curriculum and rack up badges.redeemHow To Claim Your Rewards1Complete 5 Google Cloud skill badges between 16th–20th October.2Share a public post about your 5 badges on LinkedIn and copy the post URL once it's live.3Submit the form here.4Our team will verify your entries — you'll receive your rewards within 15–20 business days after verification.alt_routeLearner CategoryPick The Track That Fits YouschoolStudentFor learners early in their journeyStart from the fundamentals of Google Cloud and build a solid, practical base with beginner-friendly labs and badges.check_circleFoundational cloud concepts through guided hands-on labscheck_circleA student curriculum of curated skill badgescheck_circleSelf-attest as a Student on the enrolment formcheck_circlePublic Google Skills profile to track your badgesView student curriculumnorth_eastGreat for first-time cloud learnerscodeDeveloperFor working & aspiring developersGo deeper with a developer-focused curriculum and one extra step that connects you to Google's agent-building ecosystem.check_circleAn advanced developer curriculum of skill badgescheck_circleSelf-attest as a Developer on the enrolment formcheck_circleSign up for the Gemini Enterprise Agent Ready (GEAR) programcheck_circleSubmit your Google Developer profile URL during enrolmentView developer curriculumnorth_eastOne extra step: GEAR sign-upmilitary_techWhat You'll EarnRewards Worth Showing Offworkspace_premium5+ BadgesGoogle-Branded CertificateComplete 5 or more Google Skill Badges and earn an exclusive Google-branded certificate that showcases your hands-on cloud skills.redeemBonusWin GfG Exclusive SwagsKeep learning and sharing your progress for a chance to win GeeksforGeeks exclusive swags — our way of celebrating your momentum.tips_and_updatesImportantImportant Pointersconfirmation_numberSeats are limited and allocated first come, first served — register early.descriptionUse only the GeeksforGeeks partner form. Don't use a personal form or a form meant for another community.visibility_offReferral codes aren't public — use the one shared with you by GeeksforGeeks.scheduleYou can complete up to 15 labs per 24 hours. After that, you get 1 new attempt every 2 hours.updateProgress reports can lag by 24–48 hours, so give new badges a little time to show up.local_offerYou will receive an exclusive discount of 40% on GfG courses, based on the number of badges you complete and your social-sharing activity.To meet the minimum eligibility criteria, you must complete at least 5 Google Skill Badges and fulfil the social-sharing requirements